# SMI-5207 governance review L-3: scripts/indexer/smi5207-blast-radius-{weekly,
# transitions}.ts default their report output here instead of the repo root
# (CLAUDE.md "Never save working files, text/mds and tests to the root folder").
.smi5207-reports/
# SMI-6441 Wave 2: scripts/indexer/smi6441-blast-radius.ts follows the same
# convention for the same reason.
.smi6441-reports/
# SMI-5879 / SMI-6444 / SMI-6481 census, simulation, gate-check and acceptance
# evidence. These tools default-write to the repo root, and the files are
# campaign evidence referenced from Linear rather than committed artifacts.
# Left untracked they fail `format:check`, which scans the whole tree — that
# blocked a docs-only push on 2026-09-09 for reasons unrelated to the change.
#
# TWO patterns per prefix, not one wildcard. Each prefix needs the tool's own
# output (`.json`) plus the operator's pre-rerun backup of it (`.json.bak…`,
# e.g. `.json.bak-pre-smi6481` on a 169MB file that sat unmatched here).
#
# Scope limit, deliberate: ONLY the `.bak` backup convention is covered. A
# backup saved under any other suffix — `.json.gz`, `.json.old`, `.json.copy`
# — stays VISIBLE, where the old `.json*` had swallowed it. That narrowing is
# intended, not an oversight: #2795's cross-family pre-merge review raised the
# compressed case, and a grep for gzip/zlib/zstd/zip/archiver across the three
# tools found no compression path in any of them, so re-widening for a shape
# nothing produces would repeat exactly the guess this block was rewritten to
# undo. If a tool ever starts compressing, add that explicit suffix per prefix
# — never restore `.json*`.
#
# An earlier revision collapsed both into a single `.json*` and claimed
# "`.json` still anchors the match". That was WRONG, and #2789's cross-family
# pre-merge review caught it: `.json*` means "STARTS WITH `.json`", so it also
# swallowed root-level `.jsonl`, `.json5`, `.jsonnet`, `.json.ts` and
# `.json.example` — real formats someone could legitimately want to commit.
# Silently hiding a source or data file is exactly the risk this block must
# not create. Confirmed with `git check-ignore -v --no-index` in both
# directions before and after.
#
# Every pattern is root-anchored (`/`) deliberately: without the leading slash
# git matches the basename at ANY depth, which would hide a same-named fixture
# or committed evidence file under a subdirectory.
/smi5879-*.json
/smi5879-*.json.bak*
/smi6444-*.json
/smi6444-*.json.bak*
/smi6481-*.json
/smi6481-*.json.bak*
